got for ideas right now.

158
00:10:54,800 --> 00:10:55,660
No way.

159
00:11:07,200 --> 00:11:10,757
If I had more of a running start,
I probably would have made it.

160
00:11:10,840 --> 00:11:12,280
Yeah, I don't think so.

161
00:11:17,900 --> 00:11:19,800
This is kind of weird, isn't it?

162
00:11:20,140 --> 00:11:22,140
This wouldn't happen in real life.

163
00:11:22,420 --> 00:11:24,337
You know, going to strange places,

164
00:11:24,420 --> 00:11:27,773
meeting a total stranger, and
then sleeping next to them.

165
00:11:28,180 --> 00:11:30,797
I mean, you actually tried
running up that wall.

166
00:11:30,880 --> 00:11:33,174
You really are a weirdo, you know that?

167
00:11:33,420 --> 00:11:34,780
Well, excuse me.

168
00:11:40,620 --> 00:11:42,840
Kirito, can I ask you something?

169
00:11:43,220 --> 00:11:44,820
Ask away, I'm all ears.

170
00:11:45,840 --> 00:11:48,664
Why did you risk your
life like that to save me?

171
00:11:50,040 --> 00:11:52,628
I can't just sit back
and watch someone die.

172
00:11:53,240 --> 00:11:55,887
I'd rather die alongside
him than do nothing.

173
00:11:56,520 --> 00:11:59,579
Especially if that's someone's
a girl like you, Liz.

174
00:12:00,560 --> 00:12:02,266
Wow, you really are an idiot.

175
00:12:02,580 --> 00:12:05,227
You're the only person
who'd think like that.

176
00:12:10,420 --> 00:12:11,980
Hey, hold my hand.

177
00:12:28,860 --> 00:12:29,917
It's so warm,

178
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:36,500
even though you and me are just these
ones and zeros in a virtual world.

179
00:12:37,500 --> 00:12:38,330
I know.

180
00:13:14,880 --> 00:13:17,097
It's that special metal
we came all this way

181
00:13:17,180 --> 00:13:19,997
for like you said the
dragon eats crystals,

182
00:13:20,080 --> 00:13:22,198
and they turn to this in its stomach

183
00:13:23,380 --> 00:13:25,027
No wonder it's hard to find.

184
00:13:25,140 --> 00:13:26,460
Yeah, but you found it

185
00:13:27,160 --> 00:13:29,097
What's it doing down here though?

186
00:13:29,180 --> 00:13:32,920
This hole isn't a trap like we
thought it's the dragon's nest

187
00:13:34,080 --> 00:13:34,910
Really?

188
00:13:35,000 --> 00:13:36,757
Uh-huh, and that's not just an ingot.

189
00:13:36,840 --> 00:13:38,097
That's dragon excrement.

190
00:13:38,180 --> 00:13:39,820
You know poop. Huh?

191
00:13:44,200 --> 00:13:47,376
Well, I guess this means we
got what we came here for.

192
00:13:47,740 --> 00:13:48,916
Still stuck, though.

193
00:13:51,120 --> 00:13:54,720
Wait, this is supposed to be
a dragon's nest, right? Yep.

194
00:13:55,060 --> 00:13:59,040
Because dragons are nocturnal, so
it won't be long before it comes.

195
00:14:04,040 --> 00:14:04,870
It's here!

196
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:09,837
What? What?

197
00:14:09,920 --> 00:14:11,038
What are you doing?

198
00:14:21,400 --> 00:14:22,820
Hang on to me, Liz!

199
00:14:32,520 --> 00:14:33,480
Almost there!

200
00:14:47,020 --> 00:14:48,057
Wow!

201
00:14:48,140 --> 00:14:49,440
Look at that!

202
00:15:00,280 --> 00:15:01,317
Kirito!

203
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,020
You know what? What?

204
00:15:03,880 --> 00:15:04,710
No!

205
00:15:04,793 --> 00:15:05,623
What?

206
00:15:05,880 --> 00:15:06,710
Don't freak out!

207
00:15:06,793 --> 00:15:08,780
But I'm falling in love with you!

208
00:15:09,980 --> 00:15:11,640
I can't hear a thing!

209
00:15:11,980 --> 00:15:13,340
What did you just say?

210
00:15:14,980 --> 00:15:16,180
Never mind!

211
00:15:26,980 --> 00:15:29,980
A one-handed longsword, right? Yup.

212
00:15:30,400 --> 00:15:31,400
Make it awesome.

213
00:15:44,060 --> 00:15:49,460
I didn't imagine it, the warmth
of Kirito's hands, the way I feel.

214
00:15:51,300 --> 00:15:54,780
As soon as I've made the best
sword I can, I'll tell him.

215
00:15:58,720 --> 00:15:59,550
Whoa.

216
00:16:13,700 --> 00:16:15,940
The sword is called Dark Repulsor.

217
00:16:16,380 --> 00:16:17,480
One of a kind.

218
00:16:17,840 --> 00:16:20,664
And it's not even in the
Infobroker's directory.

219
00:16:21,440 --> 00:16:23,420
Go on, try it. Okay.

220
00:16:29,900 --> 00:16:30,730
Good?

221
00:16:31,080 --> 00:16:31,910
Bad?

222
00:16:31,993 --> 00:16:33,180
It's real heavy.

223
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:35,540
It's a good sword. Yay!

224
00:16:36,000 --> 00:16:38,529
It feels like you forged
your soul into it.

225
00:16:46,000 --> 00:16:48,294
Okay, you held up your end of the deal.

226
00:16:48,640 --> 00:16:51,120
It's time for me to pay up. So how much?

227
00:16:52,280 --> 00:16:56,480
Um, well, I don't really need any money.

228
00:17:00,680 --> 00:17:04,327
Instead, I'd like to be your
exclusive blacksmith from now on.

229
00:17:05,620 --> 00:17:07,267
What do you mean, exclusive?

230
00:17:10,260 --> 00:17:11,090
What's wrong?

231
00:17:13,340 --> 00:17:15,817
I mean, anytime you get
back from the field,

232
00:17:15,900 --> 00:17:18,237
stop by and let me do
maintenance on your gear.

233
00:17:18,320 --> 00:17:19,150
Every day.

234
00:17:19,233 --> 00:17:20,374
From now till the end.

235
00:17:24,440 --> 00:17:25,397
Liz, I...

236
00:17:25,480 --> 00:17:26,317
Kirito...

237
00:17:26,400 --> 00:17:28,417
I just...

238
00:17:28,500 --> 00:17:29,897
I...

239
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:31,080
Liz!

240
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:32,740
I was so worried!

241
00:17:33,780 --> 00:17:35,280
Asuna? Liz!

242
00:17:35,580 --> 00:17:36,857
Where were you last night?

243
00:17:36,940 --> 00:17:41,077
I tried messaging you, but you didn't
answer and I couldn't track you on the map!

244
00:17:41,160 --> 00:17:44,840
Sorry, I kinda got stuck
in a dungeon. A dungeon?

245
00:17:45,140 --> 00:17:46,611
You went all by yourself?

246
00:17:46,960 --> 00:17:47,790
Uh-uh.

247
00:17:47,873 --> 00:17:48,703
I went with him.

248
00:17:50,600 --> 00:17:51,430
Kirito?

249
00:17:53,620 --> 00:17:54,450
Hey, Asuna.

250
00:17:54,533 --> 00:17:55,460
Long time no see.

251
00:17:55,740 --> 00:17:57,700
It's been, what, like two days?

252
00:17:58,000 --> 00:17:59,417
Well, this is a surprise.

253
00:17:59,500 --> 00:18:01,477
I didn't know you wanted
to check this place out.

254
00:18:01,560 --> 00:18:04,097
I wish you would have told me
I could have come with you.

255
00:18:04,180 --> 00:18:05,440
I'm sort of confused.

256
00:18:05,620 --> 00:18:06,777
Do you know each other?

257
00:18:06,860 --> 00:18:09,780
Yeah, both of us are on
the assault team, so...

258
00:18:11,080 --> 00:18:13,737
He said he was looking to
get a more powerful sword,

259
00:18:13,820 --> 00:18:16,055
so I told him about you and your shop.

260
00:18:16,640 --> 00:18:17,470
Oh.

261
00:18:17,553 --> 00:18:18,417
Why is she acting like that?

262
00:18:18,500 --> 00:18:20,277
I swear, if you did
anything weird to her...

263
00:18:20,360 --> 00:18:21,780
I didn't do anything.

264
00:18:21,980 --> 00:18:24,156
Then why'd you stutter just now, huh?

265
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:27,197
You know, you could try to
show a little more compassion.

266
00:18:27,280 --> 00:18:28,456
I almost got killed.

267
00:18:28,620 --> 00:18:29,880
Like that's my fault!

268
00:18:30,140 --> 00:18:32,611
Don't I always tell you not to fight solo?

269
00:18:32,900 --> 00:18:33,730
Right.

270
00:18:34,360 --> 00:18:35,420
I get it now.

271
00:18:37,020 --> 00:18:40,138
If this guy said anything
rude, you'd tell me, right?

272
00:18:42,000 --> 00:18:42,830
Liz?

273
00:18:46,080 --> 00:18:47,837
Do you want to talk about rude?

274
00:18:47,920 --> 00:18:48,750
Try this.

275
00:18:48,833 --> 00:18:51,997
First thing he does when he comes
in is shatter my best sword.

276
00:18:52,080 --> 00:18:53,260
What? I'm sorry.

277
00:18:53,660 --> 00:18:54,580
Oh, come on.

278
00:18:54,720 --> 00:18:57,132
You don't have to apologize for anything.

279
00:18:57,520 --> 00:19:00,814
He might be a little weird,
but he's not such a bad guy.

280
00:19:00,980 --> 00:19:02,537
Don't screw this up, Asuna.

281
00:19:02,620 --> 00:19:03,450
He's a keeper.

282
00:19:04,460 --> 00:19:06,519
But I told you, it's not like that!

283
00:19:07,820 --> 00:19:08,650
Liz?

284
00:19:08,733 --> 00:19:10,597
Sorry, I have to go pick up some supplies.

285
00:19:10,680 --> 00:19:11,798
I'll be right back.

286
00:19:12,180 --> 00:19:14,121
But you're gonna leave the store?

287
00:19:14,240 --> 00:19:16,257
Hold down the fort for me. Later!

288
00:19:16,340 --> 00:19:17,240
What?

289
00:19:17,540 --> 00:19:18,560
No, wait, wait!

290
00:19:25,580 --> 00:19:26,410
Lisbeth.

291
00:19:37,600 --> 00:19:38,430
Lisbeth.

292
00:19:45,100 --> 00:19:46,820
I almost got away with it.

293
00:19:49,840 --> 00:19:55,060
A couple more minutes, and I would have
gone back to my usual cheerful self.

294
00:19:55,640 --> 00:19:56,900
Liz, I...

295
00:19:57,920 --> 00:19:59,449
How'd you know I was here?

296
00:20:03,980 --> 00:20:06,745
I scanned the whole town
for you from up there.

297
00:20:08,100 --> 00:20:10,629
Figures you'd do
something crazy like that.

298
00:20:16,400 --> 00:20:17,840
Sorry if I worried you.

299
00:20:18,160 --> 00:20:19,140
I'm fine now.

300
00:20:19,600 --> 00:20:21,188
Must be all the excitement.

301
00:20:21,340 --> 00:20:23,340
I'm not used to having adventures.

302
00:20:26,960 --> 00:20:30,380
Anyway, I'll just forget
everything I said, okay?

303
00:20:32,440 --> 00:20:33,657
Liz, I...

304
00:20:33,740 --> 00:20:35,820
I just wanted to thank you.

305
00:20:36,940 --> 00:20:38,217
See, I...

306
00:20:38,300 --> 00:20:39,660
I don't know.

307
00:20:40,640 --> 00:20:44,346
I always thought dying was better
than surviving day after day.

308
00:20:44,500 --> 00:20:45,840
Living with the guilt.

309
00:20:47,760 --> 00:20:48,590
Kirito.

310
00:20:49,200 --> 00:20:53,960
But then, we got stuck in that hole, and
I was really happy we were still alive.

311
00:20:54,520 --> 00:20:58,320
I realized that even here, our
lives are real and have meaning.

312
00:20:58,680 --> 00:21:00,974
Thank you for helping me see that, Liz.

313
00:21:01,080 --> 00:21:04,017
I guess it's what I've been
looking for this whole time.

314
00:21:04,100 --> 00:21:05,100
Yeah, me too.

315
00:21:05,960 --> 00:21:07,177
I know what you mean.

316
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:08,997
I was also looking for something.

317
00:21:09,080 --> 00:21:09,962
Something real.

318
00:21:10,360 --> 00:21:11,540
Hoping I'd find it.

319
00:21:14,260 --> 00:21:17,720
The warmth of your hand,
for me, that was real.

320
00:21:23,580 --> 00:21:24,937
Do me a favor, okay?

321
00:21:25,020 --> 00:21:26,667
Tell Asuna what you told me.

322
00:21:27,240 --> 00:21:28,070
Liz...

323
00:21:28,153 --> 00:21:29,200
I'm fine, really.

324
00:21:30,540 --> 00:21:33,600
The getting over it part,
that's gonna take a while.

325
00:21:35,320 --> 00:21:37,200
Until I do, promise me.

326
00:21:38,620 --> 00:21:41,149
Promise me you'll put
an end to this world.

327
00:21:42,380 --> 00:21:45,200
Till then, I'll keep doing what I do best.

328
00:21:46,580 --> 00:21:48,120
I promise I will.

329
00:21:48,480 --> 00:21:50,200
I swear I'll beat the game.

330
00:21:54,280 --> 00:21:57,957
If you ever need your weapons or
gear repaired, my door's always open.

331
00:21:58,040 --> 00:21:58,870
Sure.

332
00:21:59,220 --> 00:22:00,340
Don't forget now.

333
00:22:00,540 --> 00:22:02,658
You'll always be welcome at my shop.

334
00:22:42,480 --> 00:22:47,340
Thank you so much for watching.

335
00:23:36,040 --> 00:23:38,746
Next time, the sword
dance of black and white.
